[Start "short-system 2...d5"]

3. Nc3 ( 3. Nd2 dxe4 4. Nxe4 ) 3... dxe4 { Takes the pawn so White has to spend a move getting it back, and Black can then develop the bishop. } 4. Nxe4 ( 4. f3 exf3 { Takes a second pawn. White gets quick development for it, but Black's position is sound. } 5. Nxf3 Nf6 { Develops and guards d5 and e4, so White's pieces have no easy targets. Next come ...Bg4 or ...Bf5 and ...e6. } ) 4... Bf5 { Out before ...e6 closes the diagonal, and it attacks the knight. This course plays this move rather than 4...Nd7, which walks into a mating trick. } 5. Ng3 ( 5. Bd3 Bxe4 6. Bxe4 Nf6 { Develops with an attack on the bishop. } 7. Bf3 ( 7. Bd3 Qxd4 { The bishop on d3 blocks the queen's guard of d4, so the pawn is free. The queen goes back to b6 or d8 next and Black is a pawn up. } ) ( 7. f3 Nbd7 ) 7... Nbd7 { Gets ready for ...e5, which frees Black's game and hits d4. } ) ( 5. Nc5 b6 6. Na4 ( 6. Nb3 Nf6 ) ) ( 5. f3 Nf6 { Develops and offers a knight trade. If Nxf6+, Black takes back with the e-pawn and has a quick, safe game. } 6. Nxf6+ exf6 ) ( 5. Nc3 e6 ) ( 5. Ng5 e6 { Supports f7 and opens the bishop on f8. The knight on g5 has no target and will have to go back. } ) 5... Bg6 { Retreats to a safe square where the bishop still controls the long diagonal. } 6. h4 ( 6. Nf3 Nd7 7. h4 ( 7. Bd3 Bxd3 { Trades off White's most active piece before it can aim at Black's king. } 8. Qxd3 e6 ) ( 7. Bc4 e6 { Blunts the bishop on c4 and gets ready for ...Ngf6 and ...Be7. } ) ( 7. c3 e6 ) 7... h6 8. Bd3 Bxd3 9. Qxd3 e6 ) 6... h6 { Stops h5, which would push the bishop back and take away its retreat square. } 7. Nf3 ( 7. h5 Bh7 8. Nf3 Nd7 { The same position as the main line. } ) 7... Nd7 { Develops, and supports an early ...Ngf6 and ...e6. } 8. h5 Bh7 { The bishop steps back out of the pawn's reach and stays on the diagonal that points at White's bishop on d3. } 9. Bd3 Bxd3 { Trades off White's most active piece, so Black's king and pieces are safe. } 10. Qxd3 e6 { Closes the diagonal now the bishop has gone, covers d5 and f5 and frees both the knight and bishop on the kingside. } 11. Bd2 ( 11. Bf4 Qa5+ 12. Bd2 Bb4 ) 11... Ngf6 { Develops the last minor piece and prepares ...Be7 and castling. } 12. O-O-O Be7 { White has castled long into the open d-file. Black's plan: castle short, play ...c5 or ...Qa5, and keep the pawn on d4 under watch. If White leaves the book, develop, castle short and use the c-file. } *
